    "synopsis": {
        "native": "Pri\u010da o Anki, djevoj\u010dici iz siroti\u0161ta koju posvoji bogata ro\u0111akinja. Nedugo nakon njezina dolaska ro\u0111akinja poka\u017ee drugo lice pa razo\u010darana Anka bje\u017ei natrag u siroti\u0161te. Put je vodi do ciglane u dubini \u0161ume, gdje pronalazi privremeni dom me\u0111u radnicima grube vanj\u0161tine, ali topla srca. Ondje otkriva bajkovit svijet \u0161umskih bi\u0107a koja vide samo djeca bujne ma\u0161te.",
        "english": "A fairy tale based on Mate Lovrak's childrens novel \"Anka the Brazilian\". The story is set in the rural landscape of Central Europe at the beginning of the last century. Anka is an orphan girl adopted by a rich aunt. Shortly after Anka's arrival, the classy aunt shows a different face and a disappointed and depressed Anka flees, wanting to return to the orphanage. The road leads her to a brickyard in the depths of the forest, where she finds a temporary home among workers with a rough exterior but warm hearts. There he discovers the fairy-tale world of forest creatures that only children of great imagination see ..."
    },
